ium\nInstitute for Great Lakes Research\nMichigan Geographic Alliance\nMicroscopy and Imaging Facility\nStatistical Consulting Center\nNeithercut Woodland\nVeits Woods\nRelated Links\nResearch\nOffice of Graduate Studies\nOffice of Field and Laboratory Safety\nIn This Section\nCareer Development\nScience and Engineering Scholarships\nStudent Organizations\nStudent Success\nMathematics Assistance Center\nRelated Links\nStudent Life\nCentral Sustainability\nIntegration of Science, Technology and Engineering\nIn This Section\nRelated Links\nHome\n...\nAcademics\nColleges\nCollege of Science and Engineering\nExplore our Departments and Programs\nDepartment of Physics\nPhysics Graduate Program Admissions and Requirements\nPhysics Graduate Assistantships\nPhysics Graduate Assistantships\nAs a graduate student, you'll have opportunities to apply for financial assistance through graduate assistantships offered within the CMU Department of Physics as well as the College of Graduate Studies.\nIn addition to providing financial assistance to help you complete your degree, graduate assistantships offer opportunities to develop and enhance your career-related skills.\nGraduate Teaching and Research Assistantships\nThe CMU Department of Physics has graduate teaching and research assistantships available for students in the M.S. and Ph.D. programs.\nGraduate teaching assistantships (GTAs) are service-related appointments that require teaching. GTAs are involved in laboratory instruction for 6 to 8 contact hours per week. Graduate research assistants (GRAs) are expected to work approximately 20 hours per week on a faculty research project. Summer support is possible, but depends on the availability of funds.\nCompensation\nThrough an assistantship, you'll receive:\nA competitive stipend.\n20 credit hours of tuition waiver for the academic year (unused hours may be used in the summer).\nTuition scholarship classification as a Michigan resident.\nApplications\nAssistantships are awarded on a competitive basis.\nApply Today\nIN THIS SECTION\nPhysics Graduate Assistantships\nDepartment of Physics\nCentral Michigan University\nDow Science Complex 203\nMount Pleasant, MI 48859\nPhone: 989-774-3321\nreturn to top of page\n1200 S. Franklin St.\nMount Pleasant, Mich. 48859\n989-774-4000\nFaculty & Staff Directory\nDepartments A-Z\nMaps & Directions\nCareers at CMU\nNews\nEvents\nGiving\nSocial Media Directory\nFollow us on social\nNondiscrimination Statement\nPrivacy Policy\nWebsite Accessibility\nWebsite Feedback\nConsumer Information\nSitemap\nPaying For College in Michigan\nCampus Safety Information and Resources\n\u00a9 Central Michigan University", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.cmich.edu/academics/colleges/college-science-engineering/departments-schools/physics/graduate-programs/graduate-assistantships#main-content"], ["", "https://www.cmich.edu/academics/colleges/college-science-engineering"], ["Apply", "https://fireup.cmich.edu/portal/apply/"], ["Request Info", "https://fireup.cmich.edu/register/requestinfo"], ["Visit", "https://www.cmich.edu/admissions-aid/visit"], ["Give", "https://www.cmich.edu/giving"], ["Alumni", "https://www.cmich.edu/alumni"], ["News", "https://www.cmich.edu/news"], ["Events", "https://www.cmich.edu/events-calendar?indexCatalogue=cmich-events&page=1&pageSize=10&orderBy=EventStart+asc&category=Event&searchQuery=*"], ["", "https://www.cmich.edu/"], ["sign in", "https://www.cmich.edu/centrallink"], ["Home", "https://www.cmich.edu/"], ["About", "https://www.cmich.edu/academics/colleges/college-science-engineering/cse-about"], ["Programs", "https://www.cmich.edu/program-finder?Colleges=College of Science and Engineering"], ["Departments", "https://www.cmich.edu/academics/colleges/college-science-engineering/departments-schools"], ["Centers & Institutes", "https://www.cmich.edu/academics/colleges/college-science-engineering/centers"], ["Student Resources", "https://www.cmich.edu/academics/colleges/college-sci